# C4b.1: the real mount. The page joined a host over WebRTC (`?signal=`), so
# the remote session is the live fixture's board, not the in-process canary.
#
# `wait` holds while a remote answer is still to come: the join and the mount
# first, then each intent's round trip and the bell-driven resume after it.
wait
assert snap remote-link == webrtc
assert snap remote-state == open
assert snap remote-revision == 1
assert snap remote-cards == 1
act session-remote
settle 1
assert snap session == remote
assert dom #gs-active-session Remote projection
capture c4b1_mounted
wait
# The endpoint advertises both intents; the detail surface offers them as
# buttons. The forbidden one is refused, and the revision stands still —
# measured by a resnapshot, since a refusal rings no bell.
act invoke-action
settle 1
assert dom #gs-remote-actions Append a card
assert dom #gs-remote-actions Forbidden action
dom click [data-intent="mere.graphshell/live-fixture/forbidden"]
wait
assert snap action-status ~ Rejected
assert snap remote-revision == 1
assert snap remote-cards == 1
# The admitted one is accepted; the bell it rings drives a resume the host
# answers by diff, and the canvas shows the second card.
dom click [data-intent="mere.graphshell/live-fixture/append"]
wait
assert snap action-status ~ Accepted
assert snap remote-revision == 2
assert snap remote-cards == 2
assert snap remote-resume ~ diff
assert event remote-bell revision 2
capture c4b1_appended
wait
log c4b1 live board receipt complete
